    "git": "Initialize each repository with the empty tree and gitCommit below (hash-object -w -t commit, then update-ref HEAD). Linked worktrees share their main repository's objects. Repository kind determines the .git directory/file layout; gitDir and commonDir spell its canonical targets. Create directories after initializing repositories.",
    "answer": "absent and not_answering describe the fake endpoint. Otherwise load file at zero-based caseIndex from project-resolve-v1/, clone the entire record, and recursively replace exact string values using replaceStrings. Then apply mutations in order: each path is an array of object keys in that cloned record, and value replaces or adds its final field. Keep the vector's implicit id when relocating its path: it must remain an implicit answer. Serve the mutated reply unchanged; never construct a replacement reply object. registrations describes the fake registry for nested-registration cases.",
    "tolerantReader": "The unknown-via row also adds an extra field, covering the combined malformed-value example in constraints. Unknown via and numeric projectId count as not answering: use the fallback and log once. An unknown extra field alone is ignored: use the registered pj- answer, pin it, and do not log a resolve error. resolveLogs counts diagnostic lines from the Entorhinal decision, not unrelated logs.",
    "rootPin": "Intent section 2's pin-writing bullet pins the resolved folder, and pins its checkout root only when the answer's canonicalRoot and that checkout root have equal canonical spellings. The two walk-subfolder rows vary only the returned canonicalRoot; via: walk alone never authorizes a parent pin. expected.canonicalRoot, when present, records the returned spelling independently of the queried directory.",
    "eligibility": "A fixture's optional home field supplies the test user's home directory instead of the real home. Home access is disabled. A refused row has null identity and gitCommonDir, errorClass home_project_disabled, zero resolveCalls and gitProbeCalls, and no writes; eligibility runs before any identity resolution.",
    "writes": "sidecarWrites is the complete set of writes, including legacy git records, not the resulting sidecar inventory. sidecarRemovals optionally lists directory keys whose stale unregistered worktree records must be removed; borrowed worktree pins are never persisted. All other existing sidecar bytes must remain unchanged unless listed in sidecarWrites. sidecarBytesUnchanged makes that byte comparison an explicit assertion for the no-overwrite row, independently of the returned identity. gitCommonDir is omitted on legacy git records.",
    "rootEvidence": "A linked folder's exact pin wins only with via: root evidence from an explicit Entorhinal root answer whose canonicalRoot equals that folder. Missing or other via values do not prove registration, even with an equal canonicalRoot in a live non-root answer.",
    "cacheTransition": "Before resolving expected.identity, optionally publish and flush publication, resolve warmIdentity, flush, and warm the borrow cache again. Then apply sidecars in place (or by atomic rename when atomic is true). recreateFromFixture removes the queried folder and replaces its .git pointer with a linked worktree of that fixture's main repository. Expected writes/removals describe the final resolution, after the external transition."
  },
